#### 2.3.1 Pre-Processing

Fair pre-processors transform the underlying data in order to mitigate any existing bias, the idea being that a classifier that is trained on unbiased data will not learn any discriminatory pattern. The *Reweighing* method described in [[17](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2503.23979#bib.bib17)] aims to achieve independence by resampling the data with replacement using weights. These weights assume that the underlying data is independent, and they adjust the sampling frequencies so as to obtain a new data set that does not deviate from the previous assumption. We can estimate these weights using the empirical proportions

